{title: As Far as the East Is From the West}
{subtitle: Psalm 103}
{key: C}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [G] | [Am] [Cmaj7/G] |
| [F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The Lord [C]is merciful and gra[G/B]cious
Slow [Am]to anger and a[Em]bounding in love
[F]He will not always [Cmaj7/E]accuse us
[Dm7]Nor keep his anger [G]forever
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]As far as the east is [G]from the west
[Am]So far he removes our [Em]sins from us
[F]As high as the heavens are [C]above the [Am]earth
So [Dm7]great [G]is his [C]love
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He does not [F]deal with us ac[G]cording to our [C]sins
Nor [F]repay us for our [G]wrongs
As a [Am]father has com[G/B]passion on his [C]children
So the [F]Lord has com[G]passion on those who [C]fear him
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
As far as the east is [G]from the west
[Am]So far he removes our [Em]sins from us
[F]As high as the heavens [C]are above the [Am]earth
So [Dm7]great [G]is his [C]love
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro}
